# Keeper configuration — all of it optional.
#
# Nothing in this file is required any more. The keeper starts with no configuration at all,
# opens its console on port 8787, and everything below can be set there instead: the key,
# the endpoint, the contract, how often it compounds.
#
# What this file is still for: pinning a deployment. **Anything set here wins over the
# console, permanently.** The console shows such a field as set by the environment and
# refuses to edit it, rather than saving a value the process would ignore. That is the right
# arrangement when the file that starts the keeper should be the file that describes it, and
# the wrong one if you would rather point and click.

# The key.
#
# It needs gas and nothing else. Every task the keeper performs is a permissionless message
# anyone could send, so a leaked keeper key costs the operator SCRT and stalls upkeep until a
# replacement runs — it cannot move user funds or change any parameter. Never put the
# manager's key here.
#
# Losing the keeper costs yield, not access: deposits, withdrawals and claims all keep their
# own bookkeeping, so nobody is locked out of their money while it is down.
#
# Set it here and the console's key field goes read-only. Leave it unset and paste the phrase
# into the console instead, where it is stored in the data volume at mode 0600 — or
# encrypted, if you give it a passphrase.
# KEEPER_MNEMONIC="twelve or twenty four words"

# Only if you chose to encrypt the stored phrase.
#
# Without it, the keeper comes back from a restart reading the protocol but unable to sign
# until somebody unlocks it in the console. With it, an unattended restart signs again by
# itself — at the cost of the passphrase and the ciphertext living on the same machine.
# KEEPER_PASSPHRASE=

# The console.
#
# `KEEPER_BIND` is every interface by default, which is what a container needs. Running the
# keeper directly on a machine you also use, `127.0.0.1` is the safer choice.
# KEEPER_PORT=8787
# KEEPER_BIND=0.0.0.0

# Where settings, the ledger and the key are kept. `/data` in the container, set by the
# image; relative to the working directory otherwise.
# KEEPER_DATA_DIR=/data

# Defaults, repeated here so they are visible rather than buried in the source.
# CHAIN_ID=pulsar-3
# LCD_URL=https://pulsar.lcd.secretnodes.com
# LST_CORE_ADDRESS=secret1lj23n74aan7nlgj6hfm45fh3gc7h2ctdplsw8y

# Pin the contract's code hash.
#
# Leave it unset and the keeper asks the chain, which is what lets it sit through a migration
# without anyone editing this file. Set it and the keeper uses yours and never looks — a
# deliberate refusal to follow the contract admin anywhere, at the cost of stopping dead the
# moment they migrate.
# LST_CORE_CODE_HASH=

# How often to harvest, restake, and — as a side effect of doing those — refresh the cached
# totals. This is the only job on a clock, and the only one that spends gas on a schedule
# rather than on an event. The console prices each cadence before you choose it.
# COMPOUND_INTERVAL=1h

# The longest the keeper will go without asking whether a withdrawal window can close or a
# matured one can be collected. Not a cadence: the contract publishes the second each falls
# due, so the keeper wakes for that moment and this only bounds the idle case. Checking costs
# one query and no gas, because nothing is sent unless the contract says it is due.
# WINDOW_INTERVAL=15m

# Decline to harvest dust, in uscrt.
#
# Zero — the default — harvests whatever is there. Set a floor and the keeper skips a
# compound whose rewards are worth less than the gas, judged from the distribution module's
# live figure rather than the contract's cache. 1000000 is one SCRT, which is what the app's
# browser console has always used.
# COMPOUND_FLOOR=0

# Leave these unset unless you have a reason.
#
# The gas limit is sized per transaction from the validator set — measured, not guessed — and
# setting GAS_LIMIT overrides that with a flat number. The price is twice the chain's own
# minimum, which absorbs a change in that minimum without an emergency redeploy.
#
# PAGE_LIMIT=25
# GAS_LIMIT=
# GAS_PRICE=0.025uscrt
